From 4d36fb57d4ac9b9376105993e2e9feee69073c44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fluorite Integration Role
Date: Mon, 9 Mar 2026 12:10:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: defer pending resolution until a background exists

Upstream-Status: Pending

After the gRPC proxy started sending `agl_shell.ready()`, NORMAL surfaces
advanced from role NONE to role DESKTOP, but startup still failed when the
compositor tried to activate a pending surface before any background had been
registered on an output. In that state layout.c raises:

  "No valid output found to activate surface by default"

Desktop surfaces should stay pending until the shell has both entered the
ready state and at least one background surface available on an output.
---
 src/desktop.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/desktop.c b/src/desktop.c
index b327fe6..6fff485 100644
--- a/src/desktop.c
+++ b/src/desktop.c
@@ -389,7 +389,8 @@ desktop_committed(struct weston_desktop_surface *dsurface,
 	    !policy->api.surface_commited(surface, surface->ivi))
 		return;
 
-	if (ivi->shell_client.ready && !surface->checked_pending) {
+	if (ivi->shell_client.ready && !surface->checked_pending &&
+	    ivi_layout_find_bg_output(ivi)) {
 		struct ivi_output *remote_output = NULL;
 		const char *app_id =	weston_desktop_surface_get_app_id(dsurface);
 		weston_log("Checking pending surface %p, app_id %s\n", surface,
